          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong virtual double category
            or
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi fc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} fc
              \-multicategory
            is a common generalization of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
          %ul
            %li objects
            %li tight arrows, which form a category
            %li loose arrows, which do not have identities or composites, and
            %li
              2-cells which have
              %ul
                %li tight source and target arrows,
                %li a loose multi-source, i.e. a string of loose arrows, and
                %li a loose target arrow.
          %p 2-cells are usually drawn like this:
          %p
            %img{:alt => "A cell in a virtual double category", :src => "/nlab/files/virtual-double-category-cell.png"}/
          %p
            Note that this includes the case when
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0 = X_n
          %p
            Note that the “empty” case of a string of loose arrows this has a single object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in which case the 2-cell looks like:
          %svg{:height => "154.559pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 202.479 154.559", :width => "202.479pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
            %defs
              %g
                %symbol{:id => "c6U1fYEwyIC1hDInenl5zvPsk7E=-glyph0-0", :overflow => "visible"}
